# K03 S5 (Codex K03-S5-DEFINITION-TAIL-20261007-03; docs/LMX_semantics.en.md#resolved-head-consumption): an
# absent head retains its tail as its body; a word of the language there, bare or applied, is an item of that
# body under its ordinary statement contract, said at the word -- never a value of the head, a field type or a name.
# Here: the bare merge as the tail of a definition in the body of a named Structure of a method, refused at the word.
Model:
    size_t: x 1U
end: Model
fn: m () int
    Outer:
        size_t: k 1U
        x: merge
    end: Outer
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
